# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Both variables are deliberately LEFT UNSET in the
# self-hosted Docker build (see client/Dockerfile). Next inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# into the browser bundle at BUILD time, so anything set here would be baked
# into the image permanently and the image would know its own hostname.

# Base URL for REST calls (health check / engine API). Points at the server.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Socket.IO server URL for realtime gameplay. In dev this must point at the
# server, NOT the Next dev server: left unset, socket.io-client falls back to
# the page origin (localhost:3000), where nothing serves /socket.io.
#
# That fallback is a BUG in dev and the MECHANISM in production. Self-hosted,
# the page origin IS the public hostname and the reverse proxy routes
# /socket.io/* to the server from there, so unset is not merely tolerable, it
# is what makes the image portable between hostnames.
#
# So do NOT "fix" the empty value in the Docker build. Verified 2026-09-15:
# unset, the bundle emits a runtime shim lookup and no origin string at all;
# set, it inlines the literal, which client/Dockerfile fails the build over.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:8080
